dialect protocol
protocol semio.object.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.semio.object.mutations
start body

# REAL binary op frame, replacing the `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut this facet
# started with (`🦀️component.rs`'s old `OpBinary::encode_op`). `SemioObjectMutation` is a genuine
# data-carrying enum whose variants embed a recursive `SemioValue`/`SemioObjectPath` (itself a
# data-carrying `Vec<enum>`) — no `DslField` impl exists or can exist for either, so the generic
# `format u8 | ordinal varint | record body` layout (which needs a `RecordSpec` derived FROM a
# `DslField` impl) genuinely does not fit. Handcrafted instead: `format u8`
# (`store::pack_rt::OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `tag u8` (the `SemioObjectMutation` variant
# ordinal, same 0-8 order `print_object_mutation`'s own keyword match uses) as two REAL fixed
# fields, then the variant's own recursive path/key/value/id payload as one opaque trailing `bytes`
# chain.
#
# The recursive payload itself is real LEB128-varint-framed binary (`enc_semio_value_bin`/
# `enc_semio_path_bin`/`enc_semio_object_snapshot_bin` in the same `🦀️component.rs`, reusing
# `store::pack_rt::write_varint_u64`/`store::ByteReader`) — NOT re-modeled field-by-field here
# because `Prim::Ref` (the only construct that could describe the self-recursion at the
# protocol-dialect level) unconditionally errors during `walk_protocol` (recipe §5's
# `protocol-prim-ref-recursion` gap). This is the same honest-boundary treatment the plan itself
# prescribes for a compressed payload segment — opaque at the protocol layer, genuinely structured
# (and round-trip tested) at the Rust layer. Same shape json's own
# `🧬️mutations/💾️binary/📡️component.protocol.semio` uses for its own `format`/`tag` header.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8
chain payload bytes
